  "identifier": "openflexure-microscope",
  "name": "OpenFlexure Microscope",
  "description": "3D-printable, fully automated laboratory microscope built on a monolithic flexure translation stage for sub-micron motion. Designed for low-cost deployment in research, education, and clinical settings such as malaria and tuberculosis diagnosis. Hardware, firmware, and control software are open; the project has shipped builds to labs and clinics in low-resource settings.",
